# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Author:        David Gilinsky
# File:          stage-nightwatcher/01-nightwatcher/00-debconf
# Purpose:       Preseed NightWatcher2's install-time questions so the package
#                installs unattended into the image. The two deferred answers
#                matter: no database is created and the daemon is not started
#                here, because both need the per-unit password that only exists
#                once the unit has booted for the first time.
# Created:       2026-07-27
# Last Modified: 2026-07-27
# Version:       0.1.0
# License:       GPL-3.0-or-later
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One space between fields, and never more. debconf-set-selections takes the
# entire remainder of the line as the value, so aligning these into columns
# prefixes every value with the padding: an image built with "string  0.0.0.0"
# writes "bind =  0.0.0.0" into the config, value silently indented.

# Deliberately blank: a password baked into the image would be the same on every
# unit ever flashed from it. First boot generates one per unit.
nightwatcher nightwatcher/db_password password
nightwatcher nightwatcher/db_host string 127.0.0.1

# Deferred to first boot, which has the password to create the user with.
nightwatcher nightwatcher/db_create boolean false

# Serve the web UI on every interface: the point of the appliance is that a
# phone joining the access point can reach it. Bound off localhost, the daemon
# requires a login for reads as well as writes.
nightwatcher nightwatcher/api_bind string 0.0.0.0
# 443, so the address a volunteer types carries no port suffix. The daemon is
# unprivileged, so the appliance drop-in grants it CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE. Must
# match NW_WEB_PORT in versions.env; make check enforces that.
nightwatcher nightwatcher/api_port string 443
nightwatcher nightwatcher/api_tls boolean true

# Started by first boot, once there is a database to talk to.
nightwatcher nightwatcher/start_now boolean false
